note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note contract 5 fresh, lines 124-126 and 4 line 87: an unrolled loop writes elements 0..7 at constant
note indexes, so all N bits are definitely written and a non-constant get is accepted.
note stdout: s[5] = 6, then the sum 1+..+8 = 36 (oracle exp/f5-unroll-all.out).
om2
fn f s edit uchar 8 fresh k ulong to ulong
for i ulong 8 unroll
put s i uchar add i 1
end
t = ulong 0
for j ulong 8
t = add t ulong get s j
end
putd ulong get s k
ret t
end
fn main to int
a = new uchar 8 0
putd f a 5
ret 0
end
